<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Găbăli</span></b> ,
		ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Γαβάλεις</span> Strab., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people in Aquitanian Gaul</i>, now <i>Gévaudan</i>,
			<i><span class="en">Caes. B.
				G. 7, 64, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 75, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 19,
				33, § 109</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Găbă-lĭcus</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Gabali</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pagus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 42, 97, § 240</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Găbălĭtānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civitas,</span>”
				<i>the capital of the Gabali</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 5, 13</span></i>
			. <i>Its inhabitants</i> were called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Găbălĭ-tāni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m.,
				<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
